# Database safety

## Preserve
- Primary keys and foreign-key relationships.
- Provenance / source lineage unless the task explicitly authorizes migration.
- Frozen or unmapped inventories during unrelated tasks (measure; do not assume stale counts).

## Mutation style
- Surgical writes only; merge JSON constraints without wiping unrelated keys.
- Transactional apply with full rollback on any target failure.
- Idempotent remediations: second execution must report zero additional changes.
- Never hand-edit deployed schemas; use Alembic for schema changes.

## Counts
- Capture actual before/after counts from the live DB.
- Do not hard-code stale PUBLISHED/DRAFT/unmapped figures into new tasks.
